Falsifies `non_volatile_memory_express::verification::a_page_list_names_exactly_the_pages_after_the_first`.

The defect: `physical_region_page_list` counts one entry per page of the transfer, the first
included, where PRP1 already names the first page. The list then carries one page past the end of
the transfer, which the controller is told it may read or write, and a list that exactly fills its
page is refused.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert_eq!(entry, old)` for the slot after the last entry.

diff --git a/src/physical_region_page.rs b/src/physical_region_page.rs
--- a/src/physical_region_page.rs
+++ b/src/physical_region_page.rs
@@ -134,7 +134,7 @@
         return physical_region_page_pair(base_physical_address, length_bytes, page_size_bytes);
     }
     // Every page after the first takes one entry, and the entries must stay in the list's page.
-    let entries = pages - 1;
+    let entries = pages;
     let room = (page_size_bytes - (list_physical_address & (page_size_bytes - 1))) / 8;
     if list_physical_address % 8 != 0 || entries > room || entries > list.len() as u64 {
         return None;
